blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the release/hold decision for a partial-region metered failure (some regions raise, others return data): treat any per-region metered failure as degraded and hold the deny unless CE independently authorizes release.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan covers 'An all-empty CloudWatch read' and 'Any exception from a metered or CE read fails closed', but multi-region partial failure falls between these","handler.py L466-475 and L670-674 currently model this via MeteredFailure/degraded -> signal_unavailable, a mechanism the plan reworks","REGIONS is a multi-region list (handler.py L85)"],"finding":"The release discriminator is specified only for an all-empty read and for a fully-raising client, but not for a partial-region failure (one region's undimensioned queries raise while another returns nonempty data); the plan does not say whether that holds the deny (degraded) or lets the surviving region's estimate drive release.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5078276eaea95f22","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach 'Release discriminator' + ACs 'all-empty CloudWatch read' / 'Any exception ... fails closed'","norm_id":"nee7d6d3fb0b9842b","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["us-east-1 GetMetricData raises but eu-west-1 returns a small nonzero total; is spend the surviving region alone (under-count -> could release wrongly) or held as degraded?"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"State explicitly what the daily list_metrics ModelId-diff guard protects now that pricing is ModelId-independent (e.g. detecting an unwatched region/new family the ceiling has never been calibrated against), or drop it as unneeded model-identity maintenance the redesign was meant to remove.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The redesign's stated invariant: AC 'every ModelId in the `list_metrics` fixture is priced by the ceiling with no fallback' and Approach 'Price every token at a ceiling rate for its direction' — pricing no longer depends on ModelId identity, so an unknown ModelId is priced correctly by construction.","All four documented defects (Problem 1-4) are string-matching/pricing defects the ceiling eliminates; the Problem/Approach sections nowhere state model-drift detection as a goal the guard serves.","The guard requires a human-maintained 'recorded known set' of ModelIds — the same per-model maintenance surface the plan removes (SEED_RATES, RATE_OVERRIDES pins keyed on model identity).","AC line 3 deliberately removes list_metrics from the enforcement path ('no `list_metrics` on the enforcement path'); this guard re-adds a list_metrics call (on a separate daily path).","Ticket 3083 comments show the prior model-identity coupling was the recurring source of defects, arguing against reintroducing a model-identity-keyed known-set."],"finding":"The added daily `list_metrics` ModelId-diff guard (warn on a ModelId outside a 'recorded known set') has no stated purpose given the redesign makes pricing ModelId-independent, and it reintroduces the ModelId-maintenance burden the redesign was meant to eliminate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f78d4706e453739a8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'A daily `list_metrics` ModelId diff warns on a ModelId outside the recorded known set. Checked: a test adding an unknown ModelId.'","norm_id":"n449ff7478197ac25","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A new Bedrock model is enabled; it is priced correctly by the ceiling, yet the guard pages/warns and an operator must update the 'recorded known set' — the exact toil the redesign removes.","The known-set drifts stale and the warning becomes noise operators learn to ignore (mirrors the mis-versioned-seed noise documented in ticket 3083)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State explicitly that the ceiling estimate is computed from ONLY the four undimensioned aggregates (never summed with per-ModelId series), and that the per-model reads for logging and the list_metrics ModelId diff are separate, non-additive paths.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["handler.py L416-418: 'Only the per-ModelId series; the undimensioned aggregate would double-count everything already covered below.'","Plan: 'CloudWatch reads move to the four undimensioned aggregates — verified equal to the per-ModelId sum'","Plan AC: 'Per-model token counts are logged on warn and trip paths only' and 'A daily list_metrics ModelId diff' — per-model reads still occur on some path"],"finding":"The plan switches CloudWatch reads to the four undimensioned aggregates, but the current handler deliberately reads only per-ModelId series to avoid double-counting the undimensioned aggregate; the plan does not state that the enforcement estimate uses ONLY the undimensioned aggregates and never sums them with the per-ModelId series it still reads for logging/diff.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"febc827598a77b348","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section ('CloudWatch reads move to the four undimensioned aggregates') and ACs for per-model logging + list_metrics ModelId diff","norm_id":"n26b234ff53e1ec3f","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reads both the undimensioned aggregate for the estimate AND sums the per-ModelId series into the same total, reintroducing a ~2x (or worse) over-count","The 4-decimal equality claim silently assumes the undimensioned metric is the top-level aggregate, not one that must be summed with children"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the Approach section, add one sentence: the enforcement estimate reads exactly the four undimensioned Sum aggregates per region and never adds per-ModelId series to that total; per-ModelId data is read only for the warn/trip log line and the daily ModelId diff, which do not feed the estimate.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"